      "notes": "Official LocalMaxxing CLI v0.1.19 remote-endpoint run against commit bc41c8ce4ce0be46b60cc4d728e1b85eee1107a1: 2 untimed warmups + 7 timed streamed iterations, temperature=0, standard CLI prompt, 132 prompt / 256 output tokens, batch=1. Reported values are medians: 19.0 decode tok/s (18.8-19.4, mean 19.06, stddev 0.21), 195.56 ms TTFT, 675 tok/s estimated prefill, and 28.5 total tok/s.\n\nRuntime: 2x NVIDIA DGX Spark (GB10), 256 GB aggregate unified memory, TP=2 over direct 200GbE/RoCE (NCCL NET/IB); vLLM 0.25.1.dev24+g96bb89286.d20260710; compressed-tensors MARLIN NVFP4 W4A16 routed experts with BF16 non-experts and BF16 KV; max_model_len=4096, max_num_seqs=1, eager, gpu_memory_utilization=0.85, native MTP spec-1. Session MTP counters after integrity plus benchmark: 896/1555 accepted draft tokens (57.62%). Peak VRAM is the max per node: 101.72 GiB target allocation (~203.44 GiB aggregate); vLLM loaded 84.49-84.50 GiB weights per rank.\n\nPre-submit integrity suite passed 5/5: arithmetic, strict JSON, Korean, Python AST, and exact-format generation; no empty output, invalid UTF-8, or special-token leakage. Model files were full-checksum verified across both nodes.\n\nLocalMaxxing hardware memory is reported per node (128 GB); the two-node cluster total is 256 GB.",
